North Korea has searched a formal end to the Korean War in 1950-53, but the U.S. has said Pyongyang must first dismantle its nuclear weapons.
Washington has also declined negotiations to ease harsh international sanctions against North Korea.
"The United States insists on 'development first' and increases the pressure through sanctions to achieve its purpose through coercion and even object to the 'declaration to end the war.
