He later rushed up to the fi fi fi firing line and led with "great valiantness" the line forward before he alone determined the battle.
Lt Col Won was killed by a German sniper on October 4, 1918 - a little more than a month before the end of the war.
Michael Vann, 72, said that his grandfather's actions were "something that I know I could never live up to, but something I'm very humble about."
He and his brother Dr James Vann also put down a wreath after the parade, led by Brentwood Imperial Youth Band.
