BMW says, for example, it will close its Mini-government in Oxford for a month after Brexit.
The main problem concerns what car manufacturers say are risks to the supply chain in the event of a Brexit unscheduled.
Toyota's production line is run on the "just-in-time" basis, with parts coming every 37 minutes from suppliers in both the UK's and the EU for cars commissioned.
If the UK leaves the EU without an agreement on 29 March, it could lead to disturbances at the border the industry says could lead to delays and a lack of parts.
It would be impossible for Toyota to keep more than one-day consumption in stock at its Derbyshire factory, the company said.
