The pillars of the province Central Sulawesis economy are fishing and agriculture. This is especially true of the coastal region of Donggala.
Nickel mining is also significant in the provincial province, but it is mainly concentrated in Morowali, on the opposite coast of Sulawesi.
Palu and Donggala have been hit by tsunamis several times in the last hundred years, according to Indonesia's disaster management authority.
In 1938, more than 200 people were killed by a sncidence that destroyed hundreds of houses in Donggala.
Even in 1996, western Donggala was hit by a snctuight that killed nine people.
Indonesia lies in the circumocific seismic fire ring, which is often afflicted with Earthquakes.
